# Power BI ALM environment variable sample
#
# Copy the variable names into the operator shell or a protected CI environment.
# The SQL host below is a placeholder; supply the actual host privately.
# Do not put tenant ids, client ids, secrets, credentials, or a populated .env
# file in source control.

PBI_SQL_SERVER_HOST=<sql-server-host>
PBI_SQL_DATABASE=
PBI_GATEWAY_ID=
PBI_TENANT_ID=
PBI_CLIENT_ID=
PBI_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Operator notes to record outside source control before PublishRefreshReady:
# - Development workspace name
# - Production workspace name, if known
# - Gateway owner
# - Dataset credential owner
# - Approval reference for dry-run only
